              "pages": {
                "end": 43,
                "start": 43
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Michael B. Kimberly (respondent), according to Michael B. Kimberly (respondent), the respondent contended that the central issue was whether the Board\u2019s censure was merely an expression of governmental opinion about Mr. Wilson\u2019s speech or a punishment for that speech."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Board",
          "citations": [
