              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 85,
                "start": 85
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Board also argued that it needed the ability to speak in response to Mr. Wilson\u2019s public accusations, but that tying a censure to a rules violation would violate the First Amendment."
        }
      ],
